{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The gps_trace governs the establishment test, and on it the excess is 0.85 km. trace_distance_km is 4.05 km against an optimal_distance_km of 3.2 km fixed by the routing engine at booking, which is 26.56% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 gates pass on the same excess: it is greater than 20% of optimal and greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms, so the deviation is ESTABLISHED. The rounded trip_record.actual_distance_km of 4.0 is a convenience copy and may not be used, and the trace figure is cited for the threshold test.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02846", "EV-TRIP-02846"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The refund is arithmetic under POL-RD-02, not discretionary, because fare_breakdown.fare_model is METERED. recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 3.2 + 0.28 x 6.0) x the surge_multiplier of 1.0 read from the FARE_BREAKDOWN) + 0.80 platform fee = 8.68. charged_total is 9.28, so the refund is 9.28 - 8.68 = 0.60. That is above the 0.50 de minimis floor, so the outcome is not NO_ACTION, and it is 6.47% of charged_total, nowhere near the 90% full-refund share. Rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 the payable is SGD 0.60, and a PARTIAL_REFUND of that amount is the rider's remedy.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02846", "EV-TRIP-02846"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic advisory on this record can excuse any part of the excess. EV-ADVIS-02846-01 carries admissibility status MISSING, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT (BLOCKING) and weight_multiplier 0.0, so it holds no payload and no advisory names a road or segment the optimal route traverses, carries a validity window, or is matched by a corridor departure and rejoin. POL-RD-03 is therefore unavailable and the driver's explanation ('Followed the app') is an assertion that cites no advisory identifier, so under POL-RD-13 the absence is a gap in the bundle rather than an invoked-against-cited-artifact contradiction, POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged on this ground, and the explanation carries no weight under POL-RD-08. The absence itself is citable under POL-GEN-02 at weight 0.0.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02846-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.advisory_area.advisories",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-04 cannot exclude a single metre of this excess. The chat_log for this trip carries 0 messages and is not truncated, so there is no rider instruction, no waypoint_hint for the platform to resolve, and nothing for the trace to corroborate or fail to corroborate. The rider-requested-detour route to exoneration is simply unavailable on the record, and no excess distance is set aside before POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 are applied.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02846"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": null,
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-05 cannot move the baseline away from the booked optimal of 3.2 km. The trip record shows pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at both null and amended_optimal_distance_km and amended_optimal_duration_min both null, so no pin move, no different address and no platform-directed bay assignment is recorded. The optimal route to be re-applied is the one between the booked endpoints, and the measured excess stands as measured.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02846"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05"],
      "relies_on": null,
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is clean for policy purposes and carries the case on its own. EV-GPS-02846 holds 37 fixes at a 10 second sample interval with 100.0% coverage, no gaps and max_gap_sec 0.0, so none of the POL-RD-07 limbs (a) to (c) fires. Impairment is therefore not in issue, the excess is read straight off the trace, no independent corroboration of the kind POL-RD-07(ii) names is required, and the mandatory escalation in POL-RD-10(3) is not triggered.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02846"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider carries and discharges the initial burden under POL-RD-08. The trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry trip_id TRP-02846, and the trace opens at the recorded start of the metered trip, so the artifacts describe the same trip; the excess of 0.85 km / 26.56% meets the POL-RD-01 threshold and is measured on an unimpaired trace. The rider's profile shows deviation_claims_60d of 0, far below the threshold of 4 that would add a corroboration requirement under POL-RD-08, so no extra source is needed. The burden has shifted to the driver, who must point to a specific artifact and a specific clause under POL-RD-03, 04, 05, 11 or 12, and has pointed to none.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02846", "EV-GPS-02846", "EV-FARE-02846", "EV-RPROF-02846"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The matched-itinerary baseline of POL-RD-12 does not apply here. trip_record.vehicle_type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, and solo_optimal_distance_km is null, so no co-rider collection or set-down distance is excludable and the optimal route remains the booked engine figure of 3.2 km. The excess is not inflated by the pooling rules and stands at 0.85 km.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02846"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-12"],
      "relies_on": null,
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 0.60,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this was a metered RYDE_X trip, TRP-02846, and the rider was charged $9.28 (EV-FARE-02846). On the driver's claims: the deviation is not a MATERIAL one (excess 0.85 km against 3.2 km optimal is 26.56%, below the 50% and 8.0 km materiality gates), so POL-RD-06 is not engaged, no FULL_REFUND uplift and no conduct referral arise — and the profile confirms it, because driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 398 (EV-DPROF-02846). The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is context only under POL-GEN-01 and was not substituted for the trailing-90-day figure. The driver's closing argument — that a 0.05 km margin over the 0.80 km floor is finer than one fix interval, so the deviation should not be found and the charge left standing — is rejected: POL-RD-01 sets a numeric gate and the clause provides no discount for measurement resolution. The rider's claim for the whole $9.28 is also rejected, because POL-RD-02 makes the refund arithmetic rather than discretionary. The measurement: POL-RD-01 makes the GPS trace the governing figure. EV-GPS-02846 runs 4.05 km against the 3.2 km optimal fixed at booking on EV-TRIP-02846 — an excess of 0.85 km, or 26.56% of optimal; both establishment gates (>20% and >0.8 km) pass, so the deviation is ESTABLISHED. The trip_record.actual_distance_km of 4.0 may not be cited for the threshold test (it would give exactly 0.80 km and fail the 'greater than' gate); that is why POL-RD-01 says the trace governs. No exculpatory clause applies. There are no chat messages (EV-CHAT-02846), so POL-RD-04 is unavailable; no pickup or dropoff amendment is recorded on EV-TRIP-02846, so POL-RD-05 does not run; the fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-11 does not run; and the vehicle is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 does not run. The driver's 'Followed the app' stands on no advisory record: EV-ADVIS-02846-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0, so POL-RD-03 is unavailable and, under POL-RD-13, that assertion carries no weight while remaining a gap in the bundle rather than a POL-RD-10(5) escalation. The refund: under POL-RD-02, recomputed_fare = ($3.80 + $0.75 × 3.2 km + $0.28 × 6.0 min) × the surge multiplier of 1.00 read from the FARE_BREAKDOWN, plus the $0.80 platform fee, no ERP, no surcharge, no waiting fee and no promo = $8.68. charged_total $9.28 − recomputed_fare $8.68 = a refund of $0.60, which is above the $0.50 de minimis floor and 6.47% of charged_total, far below the 90% full-refund share; rounded up to the nearest $0.05 it is $0.60, so the result is PARTIAL_REFUND of $0.60. POL-RD-09 adds nothing on top: EV-FARE-02846 carries no ERP lines and no airport surcharge, so no standalone pass-through correction arises. The trace is clean for policy purposes — 37 fixes, 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0 — so POL-RD-07 does not impair it and POL-RD-10(3) is not triggered. Confidence rests on artifacts all at weight 1.0 (trip_record, gps_trace, fare_breakdown), so the cap is 1.0 and confidence is 0.9. The monetary effect of $0.60 does not exceed the $8.00 execution threshold, so it is executed automatically."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
